WEBVTT

00:00:09.615 --> 00:00:14.245
Hatenkou Yugi

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.556
Tabidachi wa sone totsuzen

00:00:18.557 --> 00:00:22.027
Guzen no yona hitsuzen

00:00:22.027 --> 00:00:27.829
Mawari dashita unmei ga kishimu

00:00:28.901 --> 00:00:32.268
Totsuzen no ame ni sozen

00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:35.706
Furarete zubunure bozen

00:00:35.707 --> 00:00:41.805
Warai tobase michi wa hirakareru

00:00:42.447 --> 00:00:45.616
Muimi na koto ni kakusareteru

00:00:45.617 --> 00:00:49.187
Ichiban daiji na mono wa nani

00:00:49.187 --> 00:00:57.094
Kitto kiseki wa okosu mono waratte

00:00:57.763 --> 00:01:00.596
My Heartbreaking Romance

00:01:00.799 --> 00:01:04.836
Hajikeyo omou mama ni

00:01:04.836 --> 00:01:10.138
Omoshiro yukai sore ga kihon

00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:14.171
Kimi no Heartrending Sorrow

00:01:14.479 --> 00:01:18.416
Ima wa mada furenai yo

00:01:18.417 --> 00:01:24.879
Mazu wa koko kara hajimeyo

00:01:25.157 --> 00:01:29.992
Am | ever

00:01:33.999 --> 00:01:37.196
Don’t cross this line until | tell you.

00:01:39.171 --> 00:01:41.002
Okay, I'll be waiting.

00:02:03.562 --> 00:02:06.929
So, why are we taking this mountain path?

00:02:07.432 --> 00:02:10.026
This is a shortcut!

00:02:10.235 --> 00:02:12.669
Remember what people in the past used to say?

00:02:13.005 --> 00:02:14.529
“The longest way 'round
is the shortest way home.”

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:19.243
It was a bad idea to let you lead the way
knowing you have no sense of direction.

00:02:19.411 --> 00:02:22.313
Besides, we lost the path a long time ago.

00:02:22.314 --> 00:02:25.647
The young must create their own path
that’s not on the map.

00:02:25.817 --> 00:02:28.149
As you please. Shall we keep going, then?

00:02:28.887 --> 00:02:30.616
You just treated me like a kid.

00:02:30.756 --> 00:02:34.126
Which way should we go?
We don’t even know where we are.

00:02:34.126 --> 00:02:36.928
Well, | wish | could ask for directions...

00:02:36.928 --> 00:02:37.792
Ow!

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:39.331
Hey!

00:02:39.331 --> 00:02:42.266
How lucky. Maybe she can guide us
to the foot of the mountain.

00:02:42.434 --> 00:02:43.696
Hey, excuse me!

00:02:47.372 --> 00:02:48.339
Oh, she took off.

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:49.432
Hey, wait!

00:02:49.574 --> 00:02:51.098
Rahzel-chan!

00:03:03.221 --> 00:03:04.415
What is it, Rahzel?

00:03:16.902 --> 00:03:18.233
What the hell?

00:03:18.403 --> 00:03:20.963
Now here’s a sight
you don’t get to see every day.

00:03:34.886 --> 00:03:38.913
Thé Sun
in Your Palmas (First Part)

00:03:40.225 --> 00:03:41.693
That’s a sky burial.

00:03:41.693 --> 00:03:45.930
Sky burial? You mean, you leave
a human corpse to be eaten by birds?

00:03:45.931 --> 00:03:46.898
Right.

00:03:47.132 --> 00:03:50.533
It’s still a common practice in this area.

00:03:56.975 --> 00:03:59.705
C’mon, Larawel, say hello to our quests.

00:04:02.347 --> 00:04:05.248
I’m sorry, she’s quite shy.

00:04:06.251 --> 00:04:07.912
Welcome.

00:04:08.353 --> 00:04:11.015
Thank you for guiding us earlier.

00:04:11.389 --> 00:04:14.119
Although, we were surprised
to see you in a place like that.

00:04:14.526 --> 00:04:15.515
Yeah.

00:04:16.027 --> 00:04:17.528
That’s because...

00:04:17.529 --> 00:04:23.365
Actually, Larawel’s mother passed away
before her time and is buried there.

00:04:24.069 --> 00:04:28.569
This poor thing visits the spot occasionally
whenever she thinks of her mother.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:31.502
| see, so your mother is...

00:04:34.546 --> 00:04:35.911
Mommy?

00:04:38.216 --> 00:04:42.880
By the way, may | ask how you are all related?

00:04:43.221 --> 00:04:45.086
You don’t look like siblings.

00:04:45.457 --> 00:04:48.654
Now that you mention it,
we probably look like an odd combination.

00:04:49.394 --> 00:04:51.294
Why were we traveling together again?

00:04:51.863 --> 00:04:55.663
We're on a honeymoon, remember?
Along with that blunt tour guide.

00:04:55.867 --> 00:05:00.861
I’m searching for the person who killed my father.

00:05:02.574 --> 00:05:06.678
How can you bring that up
when you first meet someone?

00:05:06.678 --> 00:05:07.667
Good point.

00:05:08.079 --> 00:05:10.240
He might have a clue, you know.

00:05:10.782 --> 00:05:14.047
There’s a chance that the person
might’ve stopped by this village.

00:05:14.219 --> 00:05:15.846
Could you describe what he looks like?

00:05:16.755 --> 00:05:20.213
It’s a woman. With long black hair and blue eyes.

00:05:26.631 --> 00:05:28.399
Who, me?!

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:31.569
It happened about thirteen years ago, by the way.

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:33.003
How old were you back then?

00:05:33.138 --> 00:05:35.072
O-one year old...

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:37.471
Boy, you must’ve been a bold infant.

00:05:39.077 --> 00:05:41.944
| don’t remember having a guest like that...

00:05:42.647 --> 00:05:48.586
but I’ve heard of a village in the southwest
where quite a few people have such physical traits.

00:05:49.254 --> 00:05:50.084
The southwest?

00:05:50.789 --> 00:05:52.590
Isn’t that great news, Alzeid-san?

00:05:52.591 --> 00:05:54.320
Aren’t you desperate, Rahzel-chan?

00:05:55.126 --> 00:05:58.220
What would you do if you found that person?

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:00.124
Would you kill her?

00:06:05.971 --> 00:06:07.199
Larawel.

00:06:09.107 --> 00:06:11.837
I-I’m sorry. | didn’t mean to offend you.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:15.138
| have errands to run!

00:06:30.161 --> 00:06:31.423
My apologies.

00:06:31.897 --> 00:06:36.231
Taking revenge for a parent must upset her.

00:06:36.701 --> 00:06:44.233
Since her mother died
while giving birth to her, she blames herself.

00:06:45.243 --> 00:06:47.370
What a pitiful child she is.

00:06:47.846 --> 00:06:51.407
| would do anything for her.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:53.874
Anything.

00:06:56.721 --> 00:06:58.382
Sky burial, huh?

00:06:58.790 --> 00:07:01.224
| wonder why they still preserve this odd custom.

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:02.854
What a foolish question.

00:07:03.194 --> 00:07:10.498
It all depends on the cultural setting or
religious view to determine what’s right and wrong.

00:07:11.069 --> 00:07:12.900
What about the bones?

00:07:13.271 --> 00:07:16.934
I’ve heard that they smash them
to make it easier for the birds to eat.

00:07:17.309 --> 00:07:18.435
Cut it out.

00:07:18.610 --> 00:07:21.479
You’re making my lousy meal taste even worse.

00:07:21.479 --> 00:07:22.571
You guys.

00:07:23.715 --> 00:07:25.012
Got a minute?

00:07:26.051 --> 00:07:27.643
You're travelers, right?

00:07:28.119 --> 00:07:30.815
You shouldn't be staying at Jenhoup’s inn.

00:07:31.122 --> 00:07:32.487
Jenhoup?

00:07:32.757 --> 00:07:35.590
Oh! You mean Larawel’s father?

00:07:35.961 --> 00:07:37.758
What’s this all about?

00:07:38.163 --> 00:07:41.963
Going into details would disgrace this village.

00:07:42.867 --> 00:07:45.392
But you should change
your accommodation immediately.

00:07:45.704 --> 00:07:47.569
You don’t want to die, do you?

00:07:47.973 --> 00:07:51.076
What do you mean?
Is that place haunted or something?

00:07:51.076 --> 00:07:55.576
Who cares? | wish someone
would’ve warned us not to eat here instead.

00:07:55.647 --> 00:07:56.714
Stop fooling around!

00:07:56.715 --> 00:07:59.150
We're giving you advice out of concern.

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:02.916
Instead of worrying about others,
why don’t you worry about yourself?

00:08:03.722 --> 00:08:04.586
It’s falling off.

00:08:06.624 --> 00:08:08.023
Wh-what are you talking about?

00:08:08.293 --> 00:08:11.362
How could you be so ungrateful
to our kind warning?

00:08:11.363 --> 00:08:13.024
Dad wears a wig?

00:08:13.598 --> 00:08:16.158
Forget it. You'll be sorry later.

00:08:16.735 --> 00:08:18.293
Please wait, Mayor!

00:08:19.504 --> 00:08:20.664
What was that about?

00:08:20.872 --> 00:08:22.339
We should pay no attention to it.

00:08:22.774 --> 00:08:25.443
We're leaving here tomorrow anyway.

00:08:25.443 --> 00:08:27.011
Huh? We are?

00:08:27.012 --> 00:08:32.143
Didn’t you hear earlier? In the southwest
there may be a clue to my enemy.

00:08:32.751 --> 00:08:35.151
We have no reason to stay here.

00:08:36.087 --> 00:08:38.289
| disagree with you. I'm not leaving.

00:08:38.289 --> 00:08:39.556
Why's that?

00:08:39.557 --> 00:08:44.057
Because if people with my similar physical traits
are hanging around everywhere,

00:08:44.996 --> 00:08:46.759
| won't stand out as much.

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:56.172
It'd be quickest to head north
and catch a boat from the harbor.

00:08:56.341 --> 00:08:57.175
Agreed.

00:08:57.175 --> 00:08:58.767
You're not taking me seriously?

00:08:59.244 --> 00:09:00.370
Of course not.

00:09:00.745 --> 00:09:03.509
There’s no way you could convince us
with such a ridiculous reason.

00:09:03.782 --> 00:09:04.771
Why not?

00:09:04.983 --> 00:09:08.720
Wishing to stand out is part
of human nature, right?

00:09:08.720 --> 00:09:11.622
That’s just vanity. Your personal desire.

00:09:11.623 --> 00:09:13.691
| want to stand out! More than anyone!

00:09:13.691 --> 00:09:14.248
Look.

00:09:14.692 --> 00:09:16.421
Oh, good timing.

00:09:17.028 --> 00:09:18.893
Have you seen Larawel around?

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:21.630
She’s not back from her errands.

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:22.630
What?

00:09:26.071 --> 00:09:27.663
Larawel-chan!

00:09:28.873 --> 00:09:31.068
So, why do we have to help find her?

00:09:31.242 --> 00:09:34.143
Be quiet. It just sort of happened.

00:09:34.813 --> 00:09:35.939
Hey!

00:09:36.247 --> 00:09:37.781
Larawel-chan!

00:09:37.782 --> 00:09:40.148
Hey! She can’t possibly be in there!

00:09:40.385 --> 00:09:45.618
Listen, Young Lady. Have you heard of the proverb
“Many go out for wool and come home shorn”?

00:09:45.924 --> 00:09:49.661
In just a few hours,
you'll be the missing one that we'll search for.

00:09:49.661 --> 00:09:51.151
Be quiet, Young Man.

00:09:51.529 --> 00:09:56.029
Someone who can read a map
could never understand what it feels like to get lost.

00:09:56.034 --> 00:09:59.435
You just admitted that you can’t read a map.

00:09:59.771 --> 00:10:02.173
Not only that, she’s still a little child.

00:10:02.173 --> 00:10:04.903
Captain, a little child in sight!

00:10:08.313 --> 00:10:09.143
Forget it!

00:10:09.647 --> 00:10:11.137
ll go find her myself.

00:10:13.618 --> 00:10:15.853
Uh-oh, she’s gone.

00:10:15.854 --> 00:10:17.515
You shouldn't have teased her like that.

00:10:18.223 --> 00:10:21.556
| just wanted to uplift her spirits.

00:10:21.960 --> 00:10:25.663
She seems a little down today.

00:10:25.663 --> 00:10:30.259
Really? To me, she looks
as stupidly energetic as usual.

00:10:34.939 --> 00:10:39.143
Al-kiddo, searching for a missing kid
or pest control. Which would you pick?

00:10:39.144 --> 00:10:40.736
I'd rather go home.

00:10:41.579 --> 00:10:43.342
Take care of Rahzel-chan, okay?

00:10:44.282 --> 00:10:45.010
Later!

00:11:30.862 --> 00:11:32.762
Sorry, did | scare you?

00:11:33.064 --> 00:11:34.122
Miss...

00:11:34.299 --> 00:11:34.993
It’s Rahzel.

00:11:36.401 --> 00:11:37.595
You can call me that.

00:11:38.403 --> 00:11:41.099
It’s getting dark soon,
so I'll take you home.

00:11:45.009 --> 00:11:47.277
Hey, I’m not very familiar with this,

00:11:47.278 --> 00:11:49.940
but they don’t have a grave-post for sky burials?
That’s inconvenient, isn’t it?

00:11:50.949 --> 00:11:52.712
Actually, that’s a lie.

00:11:53.051 --> 00:11:55.815
It’s not true that sky burials
are a common practice.

00:11:56.354 --> 00:12:05.160
This is where criminals, individuals with no family,
or those who died from infectious disease come.

00:12:05.630 --> 00:12:09.767
Those who died in an ominous way
will be brought here to be eaten by birds,

00:12:09.767 --> 00:12:11.758
so that the evil will fly far away after their death.

00:12:13.538 --> 00:12:16.996
| wonder if those people can go to heaven, too.

00:12:17.942 --> 00:12:20.103
But I’m a bit jealous.

00:12:20.878 --> 00:12:24.541
| mean, they get to fly in the sky with birds.

00:12:25.917 --> 00:12:32.948
They’ll become the bird’s blood,
then the bird itself, and fly far, far away.

00:12:34.592 --> 00:12:39.154
That sounds like a romantic thought,
but being a human is better than a bird.

00:12:39.497 --> 00:12:40.431
Better?

00:12:40.431 --> 00:12:42.232
Yeah, definitely.

00:12:42.233 --> 00:12:46.101
What if a bird can’t fly or fish can’t swim?
They have no way to survive.

00:12:46.471 --> 00:12:48.803
But humans can live their lives to the fullest.

00:12:49.073 --> 00:12:51.507
To the fullest?

00:12:51.709 --> 00:12:53.700
Yeah. You know why?

00:12:54.212 --> 00:12:56.077
That'll be your assignment on the way home.

00:12:57.048 --> 00:12:58.345
C’mon, let’s go home.

00:13:11.963 --> 00:13:14.363
There you are!

00:13:15.066 --> 00:13:18.169
I’m glad you're safe. | looked all over for you.

00:13:18.169 --> 00:13:21.405
I’m sorry for causing you trouble.

00:13:21.406 --> 00:13:22.640
No worries.

00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:26.974
Men are creatures that love
to be troubled by beautiful girls.

00:13:27.578 --> 00:13:30.069
By the way, have you seen the white-haired guy?

00:13:31.149 --> 00:13:34.585
He seems to be missing now instead of you.

00:13:35.086 --> 00:13:37.221
“Many go out for wool
and come home shorn,” huh?

00:13:37.221 --> 00:13:38.518
He’s a grown-up loser.

00:13:38.890 --> 00:13:43.987
| guess it’s wise to hold Al-kiddo’s hand
like that, so he won't get lost.

00:13:44.429 --> 00:13:45.589
I’m sorry.

00:13:46.297 --> 00:13:49.095
| was being impudent, wasn’t |?

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:50.626
Larawel?

00:13:51.235 --> 00:13:54.602
| was so happy, | got carried away.

00:13:54.839 --> 00:13:58.104
I’m sorry, but I’m fine now.

00:14:01.879 --> 00:14:02.777
Larawell!

00:14:04.982 --> 00:14:07.250
Serves you right, Monster!

00:14:07.251 --> 00:14:08.151
Yay! We did it!

00:14:08.152 --> 00:14:09.820
Heat-tan, go after them!

00:14:09.821 --> 00:14:10.913
I know!

00:14:11.756 --> 00:14:13.553
Are you all right? Are you hurt?

00:14:13.891 --> 00:14:14.915
It’s all right.

00:14:15.093 --> 00:14:16.492
I’m used to this.

00:14:16.828 --> 00:14:17.988
What do you mean?

00:14:20.298 --> 00:14:22.858
Sorry, Larawel. You can make it home, right?

00:14:29.474 --> 00:14:30.702
It hurts.

00:14:35.346 --> 00:14:36.513
I’m home.

00:14:36.514 --> 00:14:37.581
Larawell!

00:14:37.582 --> 00:14:39.516
Thank goodness. You're safe.

00:14:40.752 --> 00:14:44.313
| was worried that the villagers
tried to hurt you again.

00:14:46.157 --> 00:14:47.124
What happened?!

00:14:47.558 --> 00:14:49.116
Larawel, you're hurt!

00:14:49.994 --> 00:14:52.724
It’s nothing. Just a scratch.

00:14:53.197 --> 00:14:54.824
You're bleeding.

00:14:55.566 --> 00:14:57.329
You're bleeding again.

00:14:58.069 --> 00:15:00.560
Your red... red blood...

00:15:01.172 --> 00:15:02.606
D-Daddy...

00:15:02.607 --> 00:15:03.708
Your red blood...

00:15:03.708 --> 00:15:05.073
I’m fine, okay?

00:15:10.581 --> 00:15:12.913
Is that old man still chasing us?

00:15:13.284 --> 00:15:16.086
I don’t know. | think we lost him.

00:15:16.087 --> 00:15:18.749
Don’t call me "old man." I’m still young.

00:15:20.958 --> 00:15:22.425
A cool young man, to be exact.

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:23.888
Repeat after me.

00:15:24.195 --> 00:15:25.184
Hi!

00:15:25.563 --> 00:15:26.830
Who the heck are you?

00:15:26.831 --> 00:15:29.095
You're totally insane.

00:15:29.500 --> 00:15:31.525
You don’t like your foreign language lesson?

00:15:31.769 --> 00:15:33.293
Let’s try P.E. then.

00:15:33.471 --> 00:15:35.302
Today’s lesson is soccer.

00:15:35.773 --> 00:15:39.402
Just one rule. I’m the player and you are the ball.

00:15:41.112 --> 00:15:42.545
Red card!

00:15:43.948 --> 00:15:44.812
Huh?

00:15:47.385 --> 00:15:56.123
Violence begets violence. That’s what they need
to learn when they're still very young.

00:15:56.461 --> 00:16:01.330
I’m not against that.
But you don’t need to be the bad guy, do you?

00:16:01.933 --> 00:16:03.298
Now, come with me.

00:16:03.568 --> 00:16:05.468
You're going to see Larawel to apologize.

00:16:05.703 --> 00:16:09.195
Shut up! Mind your own business, you cow!

00:16:09.373 --> 00:16:12.308
| have a sudden urge to play soccer now.

00:16:13.110 --> 00:16:17.240
You're all out of your minds.
Why are you taking that monster’s side?

00:16:21.185 --> 00:16:23.587
| was going to help you, but suit yourselves!

00:16:23.588 --> 00:16:26.691
Go get eaten by the birds just like the others!

00:16:26.691 --> 00:16:27.988
Morons!

00:16:29.193 --> 00:16:30.227
Get your hands off!

00:16:30.228 --> 00:16:32.594
You call her "Monster," huh?

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:35.128
Will you explain why?

00:16:41.072 --> 00:16:42.164
You got it all wrong.

00:16:43.808 --> 00:16:48.108
| was simply trying
to protect that girl, your companion.

00:16:48.412 --> 00:16:51.779
You were stalking her.
Can't you come up with a better excuse?

00:16:51.949 --> 00:16:52.847
Just hear me out.

00:16:53.317 --> 00:16:56.445
You are all deceived by that monster.

00:17:02.026 --> 00:17:04.187
It happened eight years ago.

00:17:06.397 --> 00:17:08.831
Although this place is pretty dead now,

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:13.964
it used to be a lively village
attracting quite a few tourists.

00:17:15.706 --> 00:17:20.006
Back then, Jenhoup and his wife
were running the inn together.

00:17:20.978 --> 00:17:25.347
While their job kept them busy,
they were living in happiness,

00:17:25.783 --> 00:17:29.947
blessed with a child that they had longed for.
Or that’s how it seemed.

00:17:30.521 --> 00:17:34.116
But one day, their happiness
was suddenly destroyed.

00:17:36.093 --> 00:17:38.027
Their luck had run out.

00:17:38.429 --> 00:17:41.728
A burglar broke into their inn
when Jenhoup was away.

00:17:42.266 --> 00:17:45.292
How unfortunate. Both mother
and her unborn child were...

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:49.933
Following the local custom, she was sky buried.

00:17:50.708 --> 00:17:55.236
Up until that point, it was just a tragedy.

00:17:56.881 --> 00:18:00.977
But a few days later, that damn Jenhoup
showed up with a newborn baby.

00:18:01.419 --> 00:18:04.718
Isn’t she adorable? This is my daughter.

00:18:05.089 --> 00:18:06.181
Isn’t that strange?

00:18:06.557 --> 00:18:10.015
How could the child have survived
in such a situation?

00:18:12.630 --> 00:18:15.463
That’s when everything started going wrong.

00:18:16.634 --> 00:18:22.504
From time to time, whoever stayed
at Jenhoup’s inn as a guest was found dead.

00:18:23.074 --> 00:18:26.703
In a distressingly cruel way
that made us turn our heads away.

00:18:29.046 --> 00:18:31.412
Shortly afterwards, people started gossiping...

00:18:32.216 --> 00:18:35.549
..that it was black magic.

00:18:39.724 --> 00:18:40.816
Everyone knows it.

00:18:41.425 --> 00:18:45.054
The murdered guests
were offered as living sacrifices...

00:18:47.632 --> 00:18:52.535
...IN order to revive Larawel, that monster,
who was killed by the burglar.

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:00.136
It hurts...

00:19:02.947 --> 00:19:04.244
I’m sorry to bother you.

00:19:04.749 --> 00:19:06.979
What’s wrong? It’s late.

00:19:07.752 --> 00:19:11.085
Um... What was the answer
to the assignment you gave me?

00:19:11.389 --> 00:19:16.952
Oh, why humans can live
without being able to walk?

00:19:17.862 --> 00:19:23.300
Apparently, it’s because technology progresses
to make up for human disabilities.

00:19:23.834 --> 00:19:24.960
But I’m not so sure.

00:19:26.103 --> 00:19:28.833
That wouldn't be good enough for me to live.

00:19:29.106 --> 00:19:31.041
There has to be something
more important than that.

00:19:31.042 --> 00:19:33.533
Something important? What is that?

00:19:33.744 --> 00:19:36.713
That’s a secret, because it only works for me.

00:19:37.882 --> 00:19:40.544
Don’t you have anything like that, Larawel?

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:43.646
I’m not sure.

00:19:44.121 --> 00:19:45.145
I see.

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:50.120
Instead of your secret,
will you tell me something?

00:19:55.433 --> 00:19:57.401
I’m a murderer.

00:19:58.269 --> 00:20:01.102
Don’t you find me freaky?

00:20:07.111 --> 00:20:14.517
Everyone knows it. All the guests
were living sacrifices to revive that monster.

00:20:22.993 --> 00:20:24.085
Wanna sleep next to me?

00:20:25.296 --> 00:20:27.730
| can tell you my story.

00:20:28.632 --> 00:20:33.194
It’s about my childhood,
when | couldn’t do anything on my own.

00:20:34.472 --> 00:20:34.961
Come on.

00:20:49.854 --> 00:20:52.345
That’s all | can tell you about my story.

00:20:53.357 --> 00:20:56.258
So, Larawel, are you scared of me now?

00:20:56.927 --> 00:20:58.087
Do you find me freaky?

00:20:58.529 --> 00:20:59.461
No.

00:20:59.997 --> 00:21:00.588
How come?

00:21:01.432 --> 00:21:02.694
I’m not sure.

00:21:03.134 --> 00:21:05.068
Then, that'll be your next assignment.

00:21:05.469 --> 00:21:09.701
Think as hard as you can,
and let’s check your answer tomorrow.

00:21:16.046 --> 00:21:17.308
So warm.

00:21:27.591 --> 00:21:30.355
That’s right. | must do it.

00:21:31.028 --> 00:21:33.519
I’m the only one who can protect Larawel.

00:21:43.674 --> 00:21:47.344
Tonari no heya kara

00:21:47.344 --> 00:21:50.973
Waraigoe ga suru

00:21:51.148 --> 00:21:58.350
Ussura mezameru asa ga konna ni Itoshii

00:21:58.722 --> 00:22:05.958
Dokoka de yumemita ichimai no e ni wa

00:22:06.230 --> 00:22:13.534
Mou anata no isu wo kakitashita bakari da yo

00:22:13.704 --> 00:22:18.204
Kanashii monogatari ga ima

00:22:20.644 --> 00:22:29.348
Curtain no mukogawa machibuse shite itemo

00:22:31.355 --> 00:22:38.591
Ashita ni wa mishiranu hito no yoni nattemo

00:22:38.863 --> 00:22:45.996
Anata ga koko ni iru tashika na kiseki wo shinjite

00:22:46.303 --> 00:22:53.641
Sashidasareta te ni wa wakare no yokan mo naku

00:22:53.978 --> 00:23:01.714
Tada dakishimetakute ima ruisen ga yurunda
